Separate a channel from the meaning of a remote operation (@computing-channel-boundaries: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Recover-complete-messages-from-an-arbitrarily-divided-byte-stream.lingua#r_004304223020FC2B4C22A527DB") { r_002510E9971EAFA78DDF45C715
A person sends another person a count and asks them to add it to a shared account. There are already several different events: deciding what the count means, producing symbols, handing them to a messenger, receiving symbols, interpreting them, changing an account and reporting the result. These events can happen at different times. A receipt for handing over the envelope establishes less than a receipt issued after the account has changed. Begin communication by naming the event that each observation supports.

Reuse [Distinguish a value from its digital representation](Distinguish-a-value-from-its-digital-representation.lingua#r_0849AE8813413F872ABE90EDB2) and [Interpret finite words only after declaring their encoding](Interpret-finite-words-only-after-declaring-their-encoding.lingua#r_02C6715D46F125388428D7A956): bytes acquire meaning through an agreed encoding, type, unit and role. A request to add two accepted pieces to a simulated ledger is not a request to add two kilograms or to dispatch two physical objects. An application protocol specifies which messages are allowed, how their fields are interpreted and which state changes and responses follow. A transport contract describes how information is conveyed between endpoints. Neither contract follows merely from a cable connecting two machines.

An endpoint is a place where a participant sends or receives. A destination address helps route communication to an endpoint; an operation identity distinguishes one requested change from another. A routing label alone does not prove who originated a message or who is entitled to perform a change. Our original investigation assumes one established client/server pair and authentic, uncorrupted messages. It supplies no authentication mechanism. Checks for accidental damage and evidence of an authorized origin answer different questions.

At a message boundary, one delivered object is one message, even if its implementation uses smaller units. At a byte-stream boundary, the receiver obtains an ordered sequence of bytes whose divisions into application records must be specified separately. The two messages with bytes A,B and C,D might arrive in chunks A then B,C,D; neither chunk size states the intended message boundary. A sender's two calls do not logically force two corresponding receiver calls. The next lesson defines an original small frame format whose result is independent of chunk division for valid complete input.

[Transmission Control Protocol RFC 9293](../sources/Transmission-Control-Protocol-RFC-9293.lingua#r_00164F03A32413E111F34FBA9F) section 2.2 specifies TCP's ordered byte-stream service and distinguishes it from inherent liveness detection. Our teaching channel below is a separate lossy-message abstraction, not a TCP implementation. The stream decoder and message protocol are two different boundaries: use the former to reconstruct messages from a valid stream; use the latter to reason about whole-request retransmission across a failure boundary. Do not add artificial byte drops inside a TCP stream and then claim to model TCP's delivered service.

Layering lets one argument use a lower contract without recreating every wire, router or scheduler. It also leaves proof obligations. A complete remote operation requires application validation and a state transition even if all transport bytes arrived. A local send success, a transport acknowledgment, an application receipt and a durable-result reply need different names. Draw these four observation points on a timeline. Label which component can issue each and which later failure would still be possible.

**Read and work:** use [Operating Systems Three Easy Pieces](../sources/Operating-Systems-Three-Easy-Pieces.lingua#r_009CB72626232ED2E08E80BFC4) chapter 48 as the progressive communication reading, after the earlier process, persistence and concurrency chapters. The source note records the actually inspected passages. First explain the envelope example without networking terminology. Then replace the messenger by a declared channel and identify the assumptions introduced. Develop the complete networking and distributed-systems branches later; this common block establishes their questions and a rigorous first construction.

**Continue:** [Recover complete messages from an arbitrarily divided byte stream](Recover-complete-messages-from-an-arbitrarily-divided-byte-stream.lingua#r_004304223020FC2B4C22A527DB).

